anding both the numerator and denominator of tan(theta + phi), we found that both contain a common factor [ sin2gamma cos(alpha - beta) - 1 ], which cancels out, leaving tan(alpha + beta).", "deepseek_solution": "To prove that \\(\\tan (\\theta + \\varphi) = \\tan (\\alpha + \\beta)\\) given the expressions for \\(\\tan \\theta\\) and \\(\\tan \\varphi\\), we utilize the tangent addition formula and simplify the resulting expressions.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Express \\(\\tan(\\theta + \\varphi)\\) using the addition formula:**\n   \\[\n   \\tan(\\theta + \\varphi) = \\frac{\\tan \\theta + \\tan \\varphi}{1 - \\tan \\theta \\tan \\varphi}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Substitute the given expressions for \\(\\tan \\theta\\) and \\(\\tan \\varphi\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\sin \\alpha \\cos \\gamma - \\sin \\beta \\sin \\gamma}{\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\gamma - \\cos \\beta \\sin \\gamma}, \\quad \\tan \\varphi = \\frac{\\sin \\alpha \\sin \\gamma - \\sin \\beta \\cos \\gamma}{\\cos \\alpha \\sin \\gamma - \\cos \\beta \\cos \\gamma}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Compute the numerator \\(\\tan \\theta + \\tan \\varphi\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{(\\sin \\alpha \\cos \\gamma - \\sin \\beta \\sin \\gamma)(\\cos \\alpha \\sin \\gamma - \\cos \\beta \\cos \\gamma) + (\\sin \\alpha \\sin \\gamma - \\sin \\beta \\cos \\gamma)(\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\gamma - \\cos \\beta \\sin \\gamma)}{(\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\gamma - \\cos \\beta \\sin \\gamma)(\\cos \\alpha \\sin \\gamma - \\cos \\beta \\cos \\gamma)}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Expand and simplify the numerator:**\n   After expanding, terms involving \\(\\sin^2 \\gamma\\) and \\(\\cos^2 \\gamma\\) combine using \\(\\sin^2 \\gamma + \\cos^2 \\gamma = 1\\). The remaining terms factor out \\(\\sin(\\alpha + \\beta)\\), leading to:\n   \\[\n   \\sin(\\alpha + \\beta)\\left[\\sin 2\\gamma \\cos(\\alpha - \\beta) - 1\\right]\n   \\]\n\n5. **Compute the denominator \\(1 - \\tan \\theta \\tan \\varphi\\):**\n   Similar expansion and simplification show the denominator also contains the factor \\(\\left[\\sin 2\\gamma \\cos(\\alpha - \\beta) - 1\\right]\\), multiplied by \\(\\cos(\\alpha + \\beta)\\).\n\n6. **Form the ratio and cancel the common factor:**\n   \\[\n   \\tan(\\theta + \\varphi) = \\frac{\\sin(\\alpha + \\beta)\\left[\\sin 2\\gamma \\cos(\\alpha - \\beta) - 1\\right]}{\\cos(\\alpha + \\beta)\\left[\\sin 2\\gamma \\cos(\\alpha - \\beta) - 1\\right]} = \\frac{\\sin(\\alpha + \\beta)}{\\cos(\\alpha + \\beta)} = \\tan(\\alpha + \\beta)\n   \\]\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\tan (\\theta + \\varphi) = \\tan (\\alpha + \\beta)}\n\\]", "ground_truth_solution": "\n1. **Given Expression for \\(\\tan \\theta\\) and \\(\\tan \\varphi\\):**\n\n   We start with the given formulas for \\(\\tan \\theta\\) and \\(\\tan \\varphi\\):\n   $$\n   \\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\sin \\alpha \\cos \\gamma - \\sin \\beta \\sin \\gamma}{\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\gamma - \\cos \\beta \\sin \\gamma}\n   $$\n   $$\n   \\tan \\varphi = \\frac{\\sin \\alpha \\sin \\gamma - \\sin \\beta \\cos \\gamma}{\\cos \\alpha \\sin \\gamma - \\cos \\beta \\cos \\gamma}\n   $$\n\n2. **Formula for Tangent Sum:**\n\n   We need to show:\n   $$\n   \\tan (\\theta + \\varphi) = \\tan (\\alpha + \\beta)\n   $$\n   Using the tangent sum formula:\n   $$\n   \\tan (\\theta + \\varphi) = \\frac{\\tan \\theta + \\tan \\varphi}{1 - \\tan \\theta \\tan \\varphi}\n   $$\n\n3. **Calculate \\(\\tan \\theta + \\tan \\varphi\\):**\n\n   Adding the given expressions for \\(\\tan \\theta\\) and \\(\\tan \\varphi\\):\n   \\[\n   \\tan \\theta + \\tan \\varphi = \\frac{\\sin \\alpha \\cos \\gamma - \\sin \\beta \\sin \\gamma}{\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\gamma - \\cos \\beta \\sin \\gamma} + \\frac{\\sin \\alpha \\sin \\gamma - \\sin \\beta \\cos \\gamma}{\\cos \\alpha \\sin \\gamma - \\cos \\beta \\cos \\gamma}\n   \\]\n\n   Let's denote \\(\\tan \\theta = \\frac{A}{B}\\) and \\(\\tan \\varphi = \\frac{C}{D}\\). So:\n   \\[\n   \\tan \\theta + \\tan \\varphi = \\frac{A}{B} + \\frac{C}{D} = \\frac{AD + BC}{BD}\n   \\]\n\n   Here:\n   \\[\n   A = \\sin \\alpha \\cos \\gamma - \\sin \\beta \\sin \\gamma, \\quad B = \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\gamma - \\cos \\beta \\sin \\gamma\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   C = \\sin \\alpha \\sin \\gamma - \\sin \\beta \\cos \\gamma, \\quad D = \\cos \\alpha \\sin \\gamma - \\cos \\beta \\cos \\gamma\n   \\]\n\n4. **Simplifying \\(\\tan \\theta + \\tan \\varphi\\) to show it equals \\(k \\sin (\\alpha + \\beta)\\):**\n\n   \\[\n   AD + BC = (\\sin \\alpha \\cos \\gamma - \\sin \\beta \\sin \\gamma)(\\cos \\alpha \\sin \\gamma - \\cos \\beta \\cos \\gamma) + (\\sin \\alpha \\sin \\gamma - \\sin \\beta \\cos \\gamma)(\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\gamma - \\cos \\beta \\sin \\gamma)\n   \\]\n\n   Upon simplification:\n   \\[\n   \\tan \\theta + \\tan \\varphi = k \\sin (\\alpha + \\beta) \n   \\]\n\n5. **Calculate \\(1 - \\tan \\theta \\tan \\varphi\\):**\n\n   Using:\n   \\[\n   \\tan \\theta \\tan \\varphi = \\frac{(\\sin \\alpha \\cos \\gamma - \\sin \\beta \\sin \\gamma)(\\sin \\alpha \\sin \\gamma - \\sin \\beta \\cos \\gamma)}{(\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\gamma - \\cos \\beta \\sin \\gamma)(\\cos \\alpha \\sin \\gamma - \\cos \\beta \\cos \\gamma)} \n   \\]\n\n   Simplifying:\n   \\[\n   1 - \\tan \\theta \\tan \\varphi = k \\cos (\\alpha + \\beta) \n   \\]\n\n6. **Using both results, compute \\(\\tan (\\theta + \\varphi)\\):**\n\n   Substitute into the tangent sum formula:\n   \\[\n   \\tan (\\theta + \\varphi) = \\frac{k \\sin (\\alpha + \\beta)}{k \\cos (\\alpha + \\beta)} = \\tan (\\alpha + \\beta)\n   \\]\n\n### Conclusion:\n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{\\tan (\\theta + \\varphi) = \\tan (\\alpha + \\beta)}\n   \\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "Consider a hexagon \\( A B C D E F \\) inscribed in a circle, where \\( AB = BC = a \\), \\( CD = DE = b \\), and \\( EF = FA = c \\). Show that the area of triangle \\( BDF \\) is half the area of the hexagon.", "deeps